But let's double-check if the daily compounding means that interest is compounded each day, so time t in years, number of days = 365*t. We could compute exact number of days: t = ln2/(ln(1+r/365)*365) exactly. For an exact numeric, we can compute using natural log. I'll do more precise: r=0.025, n=365. Let d = 1 + r/n = 1 + 0.025/365 = 1 + 1/14600? Actually 0.025 = 1/40, so r/n = (1/40)/365 = 1/14600. So d = 1 + 1/14600 = 14601/14600. So the equation: (14601/14600)^(365t) = 2. Take log: 365t * ln(14601/14600) = ln2. So t = ln2 / (365 * ln(14601/14600)). Now ln(14601/14600) = ln(1 + 1/14600) ≈ 1/14600 - 1/(2*14600^2) + ... = 1/14600 - 1/(2*213160000) = 0.0000684931506849 - 1/426320000 = 0.0000684931506849 - 0.000000002345 = 0.0000684908057. Multiply by 365: 365 * 0.0000684908057 = 0.02499914408. Then t = 0.69314718056 / 0.02499914408 = 27.726839. So t = 27.726839 years. More precisely, we can compute as fraction: t = ln2 / (365 ln(14601/14600)). This is an irrational number, so we'll provide a decimal. So answer: 27.7268 (rounded to 4 decimals). But to be safe, we can give 27.726839. I'll give 27.72684.

